# The define sets of default/main.frag with a Slang twin (task 0072, stage f): what the GLSL compiles with (the Mode
# defines the stage imports and the "#define" lines of shadow.settings), and for a set with TEXCOORD or PARTICLE the
# pipeline's count of texture coordinate sets (UVSETS_<n>, vsgUtil::uvSetsDefine). The content decides most names, so
# the sets are open-ended; these are the ones the default settings and the common profiles create, confirmed with
# OPENEDEN_SHADER_TRACE. Any other set draws with the GLSL. Lines are canonical (sorted, "-" for none).
#
# Traced (OPENEDEN_SHADER_TRACE, task 0072 stage f) with the default settings; hdr, pbr, gbuffer, gi, ao, sss, atmosphere
# and gi exterior; object, actor and player shadows; the weather (hdr, pbr, wetness and puddles, cover, cloud and
# volumetric cloud shadows, precipitation lighting, soft particles, weather particle occlusion) in cloudy, rain and ash
# weather; pbr material maps with parallax low, medium and high on the local Faultier stand-ins; object clusters in the
# map view; antialiasing 4 with alpha to coverage; pbr look physical; in Balmora, Seyda Neen by day and night, the
# Caldera Guild of Mages and the Ashlands.
CLOUD_SHADOW COLOR COVER DIFFUSE_MAP GBUFFER GBUFFER_AMBIENT GBUFFER_MATERIAL GBUFFER_MOTION MATERIAL NORMAL PBR TEXCOORD UVSETS_1 VOLUME_CLOUD_SHADOW WETNESS WETNESS_PUDDLES
